---
import LegalPage from '../../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { KAKU_DELETION_TERM } from '../../../lib/legal';
---
<LegalPage
  lang="en"
  routeKey="kakuDelete"
  title="Delete your Kaku! account | Kuxar Studio"
  heading="Kaku! data deletion request"
  description="How to request the deletion of your Kaku! account and all your data: what is deleted, what may be retained and timeframes."
>
  <p>We are sorry to see you go, but we fully respect your privacy and your control over your data.</p>

  <h2>What is deleted</h2>
  <p><strong>Warning: this action is irreversible.</strong> When you delete your <strong>Kaku!</strong> account, the following will be permanently erased:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your Hiragana, Katakana and Kanji progress.</li>
    <li>Your statistics and daily streak.</li>
    <li>The suggestions you sent with your account.</li>
    <li>The data linked to your Kaku! account in Firebase (authentication and Firestore).</li>
    <li>The link between your Kaku! account and the Sensei Pass. The purchase stays associated with your Google Play account: if you use the app again, you can recover it with "Restore purchases".</li>
    <li>Your customer record at <strong>RevenueCat</strong>, the provider that manages in-app purchases: we will also ask them to delete it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What may be retained</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The <strong>Google Play</strong> order record (payments and refunds). Google keeps it for its own legal and tax obligations, and we do not control it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Kuxar Studio does not issue invoices or store payment data: purchases are handled by Google Play.</p>

  <h2>How to request it</h2>
  <h3>From the app (recommended)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Kaku! and go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
    <li>Under <strong>Data management</strong>, tap <strong>Delete account and data</strong>.</li>
    <li>Confirm. If you signed in with Google, we will ask you to choose your account again to verify it is you.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Your account, progress, daily challenges and streak are deleted immediately. This also works if you use the app without signing in (anonymous account).</p>
  <p>If you only want to start over without deleting your account, use <strong>Reset progress</strong> in the same section.</p>
  <h3>By email</h3>
  <p>If you no longer have the app installed, send an email to the following address from your Google account's email:</p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:admin@kuxarstudio.com?subject=Kaku account deletion request">Request deletion</a></p>
  <p><strong>admin@kuxarstudio.com</strong></p>

  <h2>Timeframe</h2>
  <p>We process email requests, and the deletion of the RevenueCat record and suggestions for requests made from the app, within a maximum of {KAKU_DELETION_TERM.en}. During that time we keep only your user identifier and the request date, so we can complete it.</p>
</LegalPage>
